      <p class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        One of the things that makes the Rooted Learning Program so special is the community we build together. Learning doesn't stop when a lesson ends — our students build friendships, discover new interests, work together, and turn their own ideas into real experiences.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        Our clubs and activities are student-centered and ever-changing. Rather than handing children a fixed list and expecting everyone to join in, we listen. Our students' interests, questions, needs, and ideas shape what happens within our community.
      </p>

      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h3 class="font-heading text-deep-sea text-xl mb-4">From an Idea to Reality</h3>
        <p class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          A child might say, <em>"I think we should have a chess club."</em> Another wants to open a trading post, learn to crochet, or start a podcast. Instead of simply saying "that sounds fun," we ask a better question: <strong class="text-deep-sea">How can we make it happen?</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          This year, students have helped dream up, build, and run:
        </p>
        <div class="club-pills" style="gap: 0.6rem;">
          <span class="club-pill">Chess Club</span>
          <span class="club-pill">Trading Post</span>
          <span class="club-pill">Student Podcast</span>
          <span class="club-pill">Pokémon Club</span>
          <span class="club-pill">Garden Lab</span>
          <span class="club-pill">Crochet Club</span>
          <span class="club-pill">Math Mystery &amp; Escape Rooms</span>
          <span class="club-pill">Scavenger Hunts</span>
          <span class="club-pill">Sushi Roll-Making Pop-Ups</span>
          <span class="club-pill">Bead &amp; Bracelet Making</span>
          <span class="club-pill">Creative Pop-Ups</span>
          <span class="club-pill club-pill--more">…and whatever our students dream up next</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mt-6 mb-12">
          Some activities grow into ongoing clubs. Others live for an afternoon, a special project, or a few curious weeks — and that's exactly as it should be. There is room for this community to grow organically.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-heading text-deep-sea text-xl mb-4">A Community Built Around Children</h3>
        <p class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Our goal is not simply to offer more activities. It is to create a place where children feel they belong, contribute, and have a voice — where students collaborate across ages, share ideas, solve problems, take responsibility, and discover that their interests can become something meaningful.
        </p>
        <p class="community-ladder">
          A simple interest can become a project.<br />
          A project can become a club.<br />
          A club can become a community tradition.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          That flexibility is an important part of the Rooted Learning model.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-heading text-deep-sea text-xl mb-4">Learning Together Beyond the Classroom</h3>
        <p class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Throughout the year, we also create ways for students and families to connect outside of regular class time:
        </p>
        <ul class="community-list">
          <li>Monthly family socials</li>
          <li>Monthly field trips</li>
          <li>Group activities and special events</li>
          <li>Student-led projects and experiences</li>
          <li>Pop-up activities born from student interests</li>
          <li>Opportunities for families to participate and connect with one another</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          These experiences help students build relationships in every kind of setting — and give families a real place in the Shoreline Scholars community.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
          At Shoreline Scholars, community is not an extra — it is part of the learning. Children thrive when they have meaningful relationships, opportunities to contribute, and the freedom to follow their curiosity. The Rooted Learning Program gives students a place to learn, create, explore, lead, and grow — together.
        </p>
